  "readmeFile": "Package.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Add: IMessageQueueDrainingStrategy (OperativeBuilder.WithMessageQueueDrainingStrategy), replacing WithFrameInjectedMessage. Controls how much of the pending injection queue gets spliced into the conversation on a given drain -- batch it, drop/truncate it, or refuse it outright (MessageQueueDrainResult) -- instead of Operative always draining everything at once regardless of how full the conversation already is. Ships two implementations: DrainAllMessageQueueDrainingStrategy (the old unconditional behavior, now the default) and SizeAwareDrainingStrategy (greedily admits pending messages up to a token budget against the live-estimated windowed conversation size, requeuing the rest). Framing an injected message is now the configured strategy's job, applied at drain time instead of enqueue time.\nAdd: CommitMessageMode (OperativeBuilder.WithCommitMessageMode) -- Immediate (default, matches prior behavior) or OnSuccess, which adds a turn-starting or drained message right away but rolls it back, along with anything a transformer derived from it, if the model call meant to use it faults before the model ever replies.\nChange: IExecutionContext.DrainInjections now splices drained messages into the conversation itself instead of returning them for Engine to add -- Engine only consumes the returned list to emit UserMessageInjectedEvents. A custom DrainInjections delegate must be updated to add the messages itself.",
